{
    "background_story": "Eliana was a free-spirited traveler with a passion for the works of Rudyard Kipling. Growing up, she had devoured his stories of adventure and exploration, and as soon as she could, she set out to follow in the footsteps of her literary hero. She spent years traveling through India, retracing the routes of Kipling's famous characters, from the bustling streets of Mumbai to the tranquil hills of Simla. Along the way, she collected stories and anecdotes from the people she met, weaving them into her own tales of adventure and bravery. Eliana's love of Kipling's work inspired her to become a writer herself, and she went on to publish several novels and travelogues that captured the essence of the exotic lands she had explored. Her writing was infused with the same sense of wonder and curiosity that had driven Kipling to create his timeless classics.",
